maining in unshown tiles, offering minimal synergy with my hand. Discarding it commits me to a Dots-focused strategy which has the highest tile availability (B1:3, B3:4, B4:4, B5:4, B6:3, B7:4). This positions me for potential Half Flush (6 points) or better, while maintaining flexibility with the B1-B1 and B6-B6 pairs. The Dots concentration provides multiple paths to complete melds through draws or claims.\n\nAnswer: Play W2"}
